From 7a73525cb5ffd1fbfed1b5c1a6e2543b007da162 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:27:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Draft Inkling 2 decode with its DSpark block drafter
 (--dspark FILE)

Unsloth's dspark-Inkling-2-Mini GGUF (arch dflash: three layers that
read the target's hidden states, a recurrent head on the target's
output head, block size 8; llama.cpp PR 32218's Inkling path) now
drafts in strata-inkling2:

- every committed token's features (the inputs of visits 5, 23 and
  41 and the final normed hidden) go into the drafter's own cache:
  each layer's fused context row to K and V (the sliding layers a
  ring of 2048, the full one --dspark-window, 32768), the head's
  context row of the last positions; a prompt's last window of rows
  as it is read, a verify's rows once they stood
- a draft is one pass of [last token, mask x 7] at the next positions
  through the three layers (its attention on k_attn_dreg, the block
  and the window before it, non-causal), then the head a token at a
  time (greedy) on the target's head over the row and its correction
- spec_step takes the conversation's own run (lookup) when it has 2
  or more tokens, else a DSpark draft of the length that gives the
  most tokens a millisecond by its record (each draft position's
  rate, the drafts' and the verify's times; --dspark-n at most, 3)
- a sampled request's drafts are drawn from the drafter's own
  distribution under its settings and stand with min(1, p / q), a
  turned-down one redrawn from (p - q)+; a greedy request's are the
  drafter's argmax: either way the reply is distributed as without
  drafting (at temperature 1, 7K: 66% -> 96% of drafts stood, 52.9 ->
  72.7 tok/s; 60K: 44% -> 56%, 50.3 -> 52.1, over greedy drafts)
- --temperature F samples the command line's generation (tests)
- a lane that takes over a state it did not see made (a parked
  conversation, a fork, another lane's checkpoint) starts the drafter
  from there; the drafter's weights, buffers and caches take their
  room from the pool's experts

2x RTX 3060, UD-Q4_K_XL: 180K-token prompt, 512 tokens, no lookup:
35.6 -> 57.3 tok/s (66% of drafted tokens stood, 3 a step); 60K 42.8
-> 63.8; the server's prose 46 -> 52-57, edits and follow-ups with
lookup as before or better. Prompt reading unchanged.
